{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/2157-newbie-looking-into-scion","id":2157,"title":"Newbie looking into Scion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-03T16:32:57-08:00","id":2157,"title":"Newbie looking into Scion","content":"Hey everybody! So, Scion is a game that sounds pretty neat to me, though in have to admit my preferences in games tend to be shifted away from the Exalted and closer to the Mortal World of Darkness kind of thing. So that informs my perspective. I have to admit though, I'm a bit intimidated. I haven't gotten the main book(s) because I'm not sure where to start and I haven't really been able to find something which can explain it a little bit. It doesn't help that I've been hesitant because I've read about it being mechanically problematic. Since new edition run of Scion is a work in progress, do you have any advice on which books are the most worthwhile for a new player, or what stuff is frequently house ruled, or even a link to what you think are the best ways to fix the issues? I gotta admit, character sheet differences are giving me a little bit of a culture shock, from what I've seen. Things are similar, but different, scary! Anywho, any advice on this front is appreciated","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T17:03:36-08:00","id":2183,"title":"","content":"Scion is a mixture of ABERRANT and EXALTED imho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/589-aberrant_scion","name":"ABERRANT_SCION","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T17:23:26-08:00","id":2195,"title":"","content":"So, imagine that Hercules, Xena, Gilgamesh, and Cuchulain got together to fight the Forces of Evil in modern New York, where the subway is run by trolls and all the bankers are elves that hate you for being dirty and poor.<br /> <br /> That's Scion. However, the system is terrible and a vile trainwreck that was never designed to handle its own power. It's like building high-temperature insulation from ice crystals. Just not a good idea at all. So while I do hope you enjoy Scion's setting, information and themes. But you really might wanna wait for the second edition to get into playing it, if you can handle waiting for a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T17:36:13-08:00","id":2208,"title":"","content":"I don't own any books, but odds are good you're going to need the Core, if Scion is anything like every other White Wolf/Onyx Path RPGs in that respect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T18:15:42-08:00","id":2251,"title":"","content":"Scion is not. It has three corebooks, not one. It's special.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-03T18:16:24-08:00","id":2253,"title":"","content":"SCION HERO is the Core of the Rules. You on Earth. Fate is a what you make.<br /> SCION DEMIGOD adds to the power level of the game. Underworld is Opened up to Adventure in.<br /> SCION GOD you have left earth and now fight with the Gods in their Battles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/589-aberrant_scion","name":"ABERRANT_SCION","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T15:14:53-08:00","id":5464,"title":"","content":"To start off all you NEED is dice and Scion: Hero. Scion: Companion is helpful as it provides some more fleshed out systems, as well as the Celtic, Chinese, and Hindi pantheons.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the system has it's fair share of issues, but there's ways to work around them in the meantime, and if you go back to the old White Wolf forums while they're still alive there's countless threads detailing how to work around a number of them. The lore is great, the setting is great, when you've got a good group it's an absolute blast. The sheet looks scarier than it actually is (Deities give you favored abilities ala Exalted, and all the boxes under attributes track your Epic attribute If you've played Exalted 2E or much NWoD, you shouldn't have any issue converting to the Scion system, it pretty much follows the standard white wolf formula of system tweaks (WoD was tweaked into Exalted, which was tweaked into NWoD, which was tweaked back into Exalted 2E, which was tweaked into Scion)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><b><i>Exalted Behind a Screen of Jade, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar</i>, Good Sitting Dog, Best Lurking Cat with Bones, Pioneer Pooch, Corsair, <i>Director, Keeper of the Karstein Manor</i>, Scion with Shield of Knowledge, Erymanthian Boar,<i> Seeking Awakened, Cloaked Changeling, Family Head, Kindred, Agent, Poltergeist</i>, Disciple of the Antler Crown, Wraith, Conspiracy Theorist, <i>First Time Traveler</i></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/882-samuraimujuru","name":"SamuraiMujuru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar882_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1129"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T06:42:53-08:00","id":9630,"title":"","content":"Hey and welcome! Rules/fixes-wise:<ul><li>As characters increase in power (generally once they get above Hero) the disparity between Epic Attributes becomes increasingly problematic, and there ends up being an arms race for the highest Epic Strength/Dexterity/Stamina. Fall behind behind by more than a point or so and your opponent will effortlessly squish you/evade you/ignore your attacks due to all their auto successes. My personal fix for this is to have people use relative Epic Attributes against each other:<ul><li>That is, if Character 1 has Epic Dex 4 and character 2 has Epic Dex 6, for purposes of Dex contests between them treat Character 1 as having no Epic Dex successes and Character 2 as having Epic Dex 2 worth of auto successes. Slightly more bookkeeping but I think it stops the stats issue becoming quite so problematic.</li> </ul></li> <li>The Boons are not remotely balanced against each other power-level wise. Either accept this and pick them partly for flavor, accept it and min-max accordingly or adjust their effects to something you feel is a bit more reasonable in relation to other Boons of the same level.</li> <li>The Epic Social Knacks tend to either be interpreted as being irresistible or only costing 1 willpower to resist. You may be okay with this, depending on how much focus you have on social characters, or you may want to houserule WP costs for a few of them, similar to UMI resistance costs in Exalted.</li> <li>Some of the other Knacks are occasionally a little wonky, like the dodge DV boosting one, but once you see them in play it shouldn't take long to spot the ones that break for your game and houserule them into something more bearable.</li> <li>A lot of people award Legend based on actions or campaign progression rather than on XP spend. Otherwise it becomes a pretty punishing tax on advancement.</li> </ul>Basically, it plays pretty OK at Hero level but gets more and problematic as you go up in Legend. You can houserule it into something usable if you're willing to fudge rules when necessary, but there is a lot of hope that the new edition will give something with a more mechanically sound base to start from/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/630-vidiian","name":"Vidiian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}